---
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
const carris = [
  { t: 'Sintra and Cabo da Roca', x: 'Line 1624, Cascais (Terminal) to Portela de Sintra (Estação Norte, the north train station) via Cabo da Roca. VERIFIED that the line exists, from the Carris Metropolitana line list. I did not see its timetable or stops. Line 1253, Sintra (Estação) via Cabo da Roca, is a loop that starts in Sintra.' },
  { t: 'Sintra (other)', x: 'Lines 1620, 1621 and 1623 run from Cascais (Terminal) to Portela de Sintra (Estação Sul, the south train station). 1621 goes via CascaiShopping (Terminal). VERIFIED that they exist.' },
  { t: 'Sintra: "Estação Sul" or "Estação Norte"?', x: 'Per the line names, 1620, 1621 and 1623 end at Portela de Sintra (Estação Sul, south station), and 1624 (the Cabo da Roca line) ends at Portela de Sintra (Estação Norte, north station). I could not find an official page that says what each stop is for or how it connects to Sintra town, so why to choose one is NOT CONFIRMED. Check the stop on the Carris Metropolitana app before you go. See Getting around Sintra below for what happens once you arrive.' },
  { t: 'The mall (CascaiShopping)', x: 'Line 1621 above runs via CascaiShopping, and 1626 runs CascaiShopping (Terminal) to Portela de Sintra. VERIFIED that they exist. These are long-distance lines, so for a local trip to the mall use MobiCascais.' },
  { t: 'Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida)', x: 'No Carris Metropolitana line to Hospital de Cascais turned up in the lines I read, and the stop lists were not readable. NOT CONFIRMED. Check the Carris Metropolitana app.' },
  { t: 'CUF Cascais (Hospital CUF Cascais, Rua Fernão Lopes 60)', x: 'Closest stop I found with a Carris Metropolitana tag: "Colégio Quadrante" (Carris stop 050259) on Av. Eng. Adelino Amaro da Costa, about 150 m in a straight line from the hospital\'s map point. It is tagged for line 1624 (Cascais to Sintra via Cabo da Roca). REASONABLY TRUE-UNVERIFIED: this comes from OpenStreetMap volunteer tags, not an official page. The tags may be incomplete or for one direction only. Check the stop in the Carris Metropolitana app.' },
];
const mobi = [
  { t: 'Guincho (the beach)', x: 'M05 (via Quinta da Marinha), M15 (via Areia) and M43 run from Cascais train station as loops (circular) and are listed as going via or to Guincho. VERIFIED from the MobiCascais line list. I did not read the stop lists.' },
  { t: 'Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida)', x: 'M40 starts at Hospital de Cascais and loops through Alcabideche and Malveira da Serra, and M31 is listed as Carcavelos train station to the hospital. VERIFIED for those two line names. I did not confirm a direct line from Cascais Terminal.' },
  { t: 'The mall (CascaiShopping)', x: 'M03 (loop via Torre), M29 (from São João do Estoril station), M38 (from Estoril station) and M01 (from Parede) are listed as serving it. PROBABLY TRUE. I could not confirm a numbered line straight from Cascais Terminal.' },
  { t: 'Estoril and the casino', x: 'M06, M07, M11, M12 and M13 run between Cascais Terminal and Estoril train station. VERIFIED for the line list. I could not confirm which stop is nearest the Casino Estoril.' },
  { t: 'CUF Cascais (Hospital CUF Cascais, Rua Fernão Lopes 60)', x: 'Closest stop I found: "Rua Eça de Queiroz" (MobiCascais stop 20895), about 85 m in a straight line from the hospital\'s map point, tagged for M09 and M22. A second stop on Av. Eng. Adelino Amaro da Costa, "Colégio Quadrante" (stop 20886, about 150 m), is tagged M02 and M14. REASONABLY TRUE-UNVERIFIED: OpenStreetMap volunteer tags, not an official page, and the map point comes from the link on cuf.pt. Check in the MobiCascais app.' },
];
---
<section id="cascais-buses" class="visit buses" aria-label="Buses from Cascais Terminal">
  <h2>Buses from Cascais Terminal</h2>
  <p class="muted"><strong>Carris Metropolitana and MobiCascais are two separate bus networks</strong> with their own line numbers, timetables and apps. MobiCascais is the Cascais council's system. I did not confirm whether a ticket or card from one works on the other, so check before you rely on it. People who live, work or study in Cascais ride MobiCascais free with a Viver Cascais card. I assumed CascaiShopping, Hospital de Cascais (Dr. José de Almeida) and CUF Cascais. Line numbers change, so check the apps.</p>
  <div class="bus-cols">
    <div class="bus-col">
      <h3><span class="ic"><Icon name="bus" /></span>Carris Metropolitana</h3>
      {carris.map(r => <div class="bus-row"><h4>{r.t}</h4><p>{r.x}</p></div>)}
    </div>
    <div class="bus-col">
      <h3><span class="ic"><Icon name="bus" /></span>MobiCascais <small>(local Cascais system, M lines)</small></h3>
      {mobi.map(r => <div class="bus-row"><h4>{r.t}</h4><p>{r.x}</p></div>)}
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="bus-note"><strong>International schools:</strong> most run their own school buses. Of the lines above, M17 ends at Bairro da Cadeia do Linhó, and CAISL and TASIS both have Linhó addresses, but I could not confirm that M17 stops at either school. St. Dominic's says M16, M36, 1608 and 1609 are nearby. Carris Metropolitana lines 1620, 1621, 1623 and 1624 run from Cascais Terminal to Sintra, but I could not get their stop names, so it is NOT CONFIRMED that any of them stops near CAISL or TASIS. See <a href="#cascais-schools">International schools nearby</a>.</p>
  <p class="totop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to top</a></p>
</section>
<style is:global>
  .buses { margin:1.4rem 0; }
  .buses h2 { font-size:1.15rem; margin:0 0 .2rem; }
  .buses > p { margin:0 0 .7rem; font-size:.92rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .bus-cols { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.8rem; align-items:start; }
  .bus-col { background:var(--teal-soft); border-radius:20px; padding:.8rem .9rem; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:.5rem; }
  .bus-col h3 { display:flex; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.5rem; margin:0; font-size:1.02rem; color:var(--teal); }
  .bus-col h3 small { font-weight:600; font-size:.8rem; }
  .bus-col .ic { display:grid; place-items:center; flex:none; width:2rem; height:2rem; border-radius:50%; background:var(--surface); color:var(--teal); } .bus-col .ic .i { --s:1.1rem; }
  .bus-row { background:var(--surface); border-radius:14px; padding:.55rem .85rem; }
  .bus-row h4 { margin:0 0 .15rem; font-size:.95rem; color:var(--teal); }
  .bus-row p { margin:0; font-size:.9rem; line-height:1.5; }
  .bus-note { margin:.7rem 0 0; font-size:.9rem; line-height:1.5; }
  @media (max-width:700px){ .bus-cols { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); } }
</style>
